 ### [Large Steps reparameterization](13132-large-steps-reparameterization.md)
-Large Steps reparameterization is a gradient preconditioning technique for inverse rendering of geometry that handles sparse silhouette gradients and prevents mesh topology errors such as flipped triangles. It achieves fast convergence by preconditioning the bias of gradient steps toward smooth solutions without enforcing smoothness in the final result. It sets itself apart from standard optimizers by treating the optimization as a spatiotemporal process using Laplacian smoothing and infinity-norm filtering.
